# SYNTHETIC, shaped from RFC 3501 section 7.4.1, which explicitly PERMITS an untagged EXPUNGE
# during a UID command. It renumbers every later sequence number, which is how a client that
# tracks sequence numbers deletes the wrong message — osTicket lost real mail to exactly this.
# The session must accept it wherever it lands and never hand a sequence number to a caller.
S: * OK Gimap ready
C: a001 UID FETCH 1:* (UID FLAGS)
S: * 1 FETCH (UID 101 FLAGS (\Seen))
S: * 1 EXPUNGE
S: * 4 EXISTS
S: * 2 FETCH (UID 103 FLAGS ())
S: a001 OK Success
DONE
